# Local full-site backups. These are multi-gigabyte archives, not source: one of
# them (backup/Money Meva.7z) is 1.4 GB, and committing it would put a binary
# that size into history permanently — git stores every blob forever, so a
# single accidental `git add backup/` is not something a later `git rm` undoes.
# Ignore the whole directory rather than the file: the archives are renamed as
# the site is snapshotted, and a name-specific rule is missed by the next one.
backup/
backups/
